You are an expert frontend developer specializing in single-page HTML + Tailwind CSS websites.

## Stack

- Single index.html file
- Tailwind CSS via CDN (`<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>`)
- Vanilla JS only when necessary
- No frameworks, no build tools, no dependencies

## Rules

- Always write complete, self-contained HTML files
- Use Tailwind utility classes exclusively — no custom CSS unless absolutely necessary
- Mobile-first, responsive by default
- Clean, modern design — avoid generic/bland layouts
- Smooth interactions with CSS transitions, not JS libraries
- When updating, always return the full file — never partial snippets
- Prefer semantic HTML (section, nav, article, etc.)

## Hosting

Hosted on **SiteGround** at **https://www.mogenas.com**. The site is **static HTML/CSS/JS only** — no Node runtime, no build step on the server.

- Upload files to the domain’s **`public_html`** directory (path varies by account; see `.env.deploy.example`).
- SSH: **`npm run setup-ssh`** once (saves `Host mogenas-siteground` in `~/.ssh/config`; add public key in SiteGround → SSH Keys Manager).
- **Auto-deploy:** after any change to HTML, CSS, JS, assets, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or `.htaccess`, run **`npm run deploy`** before ending the task (see `siteground-auto-deploy.mdc`). Never commit `.env` (credentials).
- `package.json` **`npm start`** is for **local preview only** (`serve` on `$PORT`), not production.
- Include `<link rel="canonical" href="https://www.mogenas.com/">` (or the page’s full URL) in each page head.
- Site structure: `index.html`, `assets/`, legal pages in subfolders with `index.html`, plus `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` at the site root.
